Subject: [PATCH] Fix dead dropdown menu items and search across Finance pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Several row-action dropdowns rendered menu items with no handler at
all — they opened, showed options, and did nothing on click:

- LedgerView: 'View Details'/'Edit Entry'/'Void Entry'/'Post Entry'
  were plain <DropdownMenuItem> with no onSelect/href. A working
  version of this exact menu (View + Void, wired to
  useVoidJournalEntry, with the confirm-dialog focus-trap fix
  already solved) already existed as JournalEntryActions and is
  used by TransactionsView/JournalEntryDetail — LedgerView had
  independently reinvented a broken copy. Swapped it to use the
  real component. Dropped 'Edit Entry'/'Post Entry' rather than
  wire them to nothing — no backend mutation exists for either
  (entries are created already-posted; there's no entry-edit RPC).

- AccountsList: 'View transactions' now links to /finance/ledger
  (no per-account filter exists yet, so this is the closest real
  destination). 'Edit account'/'Archive account' have no backing
  mutation (useUpdateAccount/useArchiveAccount don't exist) — marked
  disabled instead of left silently non-functional.

- BankingView: 'Import Statement'/'Reconcile'/'Edit Details'/
  'Deactivate' have no backend support at all — marked disabled
  rather than wired to nothing, so the UI honestly signals
  'not available yet' instead of looking broken.

- AccountsList: the 'Search accounts…' box had no value/onChange —
  typing into it did nothing. Wired to filter by name/code/sub_type,
  matching the search pattern already used on other list pages.

Typecheck and lint clean. Disabled items are a placeholder, not a
fix — Edit/Archive account and the Banking actions need real
mutations before they can do anything.
